{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Fighting the Competition"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Opportunities & Threats"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Grammar - part 1 > Twins After All"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le09ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Language for Making and Responding to Suggestions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In the business world, at times, you have an idea, a suggestion or plan that you think could work for your company. It is important to use proper language to offer those ideas for someone to consider. Here is some language you can use for making and responding to recommendations."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Making Suggestions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Responding to Suggestions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You could ... * </br> You might want to ... *</br> If I were you, I'd ... *</br>   It's generally best / a good idea to ... *</br>   One idea is to ... * </br>   I'd like to suggest / recommend  ... * </br>   Why don't we ... ? </p>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">* These expressions are followed by a bare infinitive (verb without \u2018to')</span> </p>  In my experience, ... ** works really well. </br> Have you tried ... ? **</p>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">** These expressions are followed by a noun or -ing form. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"That's not a bad idea. </br> I agree.</br> I like the sound of that. </br> That's a good idea. </br> This sounds great. </br> That would be great. </br>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">NOTE:</span> It is important to use the word \u2018suggest' correctly when speaking. The word \u2018suggest' is never followed by an infinitive. We use the pattern \u201csuggest doing something\u201d."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">\u2717 Janet <del>suggested to make</del> changes to the proposal.</br> \u2713 Janet suggested making changes to the proposal.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">I'd like to suggest</span> making changes that would increase our chances of winning this bid."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">That would be great</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Our staff could</span> do with some cultural awareness training."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Why don't we</span> rearrange some of our current members?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "If Clauses (first conditional)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When we want to express real or very possible future situations and their results, we use an \u201cIf clause\u201d. </p>  A conditional clause is made up of two clauses: A <span class=\"strong\">condition</span> clause and a <span class=\"strong\">result</span> clause. Here's how we structure a conditional clause:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Condition</span> clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Result</span> clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">If</span> + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span> + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">verb</span> (Simple Present)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span> + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will</span> / <span class=\\\"strong\\\">be going to</span> + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">verb</span> (Simple Present)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">NOTE</span>: You can flip the two clauses so that the result comes first."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we use the resources we have more effectively, we will rise to the challenge. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our business will succeed if we keep an eye on our spendings."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we make the right move, we are going to be successful."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "representative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person or organization chosen or appointed to act or speak for someone else"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am the PR representative for the company."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when discussing ways to improve a company."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rise to the challenge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to accept a challenge"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We will rise to the challenge."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reorganize"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to change the way in which something is organized"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Why don't we reorganize some of the roles our members hold?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "expenses"}, {"type": "definition", "content"